  // Advance while autonomy HAS the boat, or is being OFFERED it.
  // The second clause breaks the bootstrap deadlock: pBBPID is
  // not valid until this script posts DESIRED_*, and the arbiter
  // does not select AUTONOMY until pBBPID is valid -- but while
  // CH6 is in AUTO with nothing commanding, the arbiter says
  // exactly stop=AUTONOMY_INVALID, which is the offer. An RC
  // takeover (authority=RC, stop=NONE) freezes the clock;
  // ALL_STOP and a quiet pBBPID pause the block too.
  //
  // EXACTLY TWO parenthesized clauses: lib_logic rejects a flat
  // three-way 'or' (the right side of the first 'or' must itself
  // be globally parenthesized) -- and uTimerScript then runs
  // UNCONDITIONED on the bad line. Seen 2026-08-27.
  condition   = (BB_CMD_AUTHORITY = AUTONOMY) or (BB_CMD_STOP_REASON = AUTONOMY_INVALID)

